_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 26
---
order: 26
---
short_label: X.26
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: A medial area does not exceed a medial area by a rational area.
----
proof:

If possible, let the medial area {AB|ABh} exceed the medial area {AC|ACh} by the rational area {DB|BDh}.

Set out a rational straight line {EF}. Apply to {EF} the rectangular parallelogram {FH|FHh} equal to {AB|ABh} producing {EH} as breadth. Subtract the rectangle {FG|FGh} equal to {AC|ACh}. Then the remainder {BD|BDh} equals the remainder {KH|KHh}.

But {DB|BDh} is rational, therefore {KH|KHh} is also rational.

Since each of the rectangles {AB|ABh} and {AC|ACh} is medial, and {AB|ABh} equals {FH|FHh} while {AC|ACh} equals {FG|FGh}, therefore each of the rectangles {FH|FHh} and {FG|FGh} is also medial.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="220" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.26 diagram" src="propX26.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the medial area AB split into AC (cyan) and the
    // remainder BD (pink); to the right the rational line EF with FH applied
    // to it, drawn as FG (cyan) over the remainder HK (pink). AB and FH are
    // never drawn as single polygons, so they, and the four filled areas,
    // are lit through faceless, strokeless twins ABh, ACh, BDh, FHh, FGh,
    // KHh (#140); prose and captions reach them with the display override
    // ({AB|ABh}, {DB|BDh}, {KH|KHh}, …). The sides EF, EH, EG, GH are
    // transparent highlight targets (;0;0;0). FHs is a solid pink twin of
    // the whole FH, hidden at rest (initiallyHidden), so "Apply FH" shows
    // the area before "Subtract FG" divides it. Resting figure unchanged.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C (given), E, F and
    // the offscreen frees (O sits invisible at the corner). E and F arrive
    // with "Set out a rational straight line EF", so they are deferred; D,
    // G, H, K are derived and follow the visible sets.
    //
    // A reductio: the construction rests on the supposition, so the closing
    // slide withdraws it and leaves the given areas.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","D","AC","BD","ABh","ACh","BDh"];
    var EFS   = GIVEN.concat(["E","F","EF"]);
    var FHS   = EFS.concat(["H","EH","FHs","FHh"]);
    var ALL   = EFS.concat(["H","EH","FHh","G","K","FG","FGh","HK","KHh","EG","GH"]);
    geomlib.init({
